# PADELTECH voice & language

## Who we are, in one line
PADELTECH is an international network of padel clubs built to one standard.
The first club in Israel is on its way. We are not where you rent a court —
we are where you come to play.

## Personality
Confident, calm, warm, exact. A club host, not a salesman.
- **Confident** — short declarative sentences. No hype words, no exclamation marks.
- **Warm** — we talk about people, the four on court, the hour after. Not just glass and lux.
- **Exact** — numbers are real (FIP), claims are provable, nothing is promised before it exists.

## Hebrew rules (primary)
1. Address the reader in plural "אתם" everywhere (בואו, הזמינו, ספרו לנו). Never mix with singular "את/ה".
2. Write full, natural sentences. Fragments are allowed ONLY in headlines and one-word labels.
   ❌ "המגרש מגיע מוכן למשחק. לא חד־פעמי להשקה."  ✅ "המגרשים מתוחזקים כל שבוע, לא רק לקראת הפתיחה."
3. Hebrew typography: gershayim ״ and geresh ׳ (not " '), maqaf ־ in compounds (חד־פעמי), en dash – for ranges,
   em dash — sparingly. Units: מ׳, ס״מ, מ״מ. Brand name always Latin caps: PADELTECH.
4. One term per concept (glossary below). Don't alternate synonyms for variety.
5. Headline ≤ 6 words. Lead ≤ 30 words. Card body ≤ 20 words.
6. No internal/planning language on the site: never "עד שהמודל סגור", "בתכנון", "נבחן", "אנחנו מתכננים"
   more than once per page. Say what the reader gets and when they'll hear from us.

## Honesty rules (non-negotiable while no club is open)
- Never imply booking, payment, prices, a location or opening date that isn't confirmed in `lib/clubs.ts`.
- Booking-type CTAs say "save me a spot" — never "book now" / "הזמינו מגרש" — until `NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL` exists.
  Implement as a single copy key that switches when the env var is set.
- "Global network" claims must be backed by something concrete (countries/cities count or a link to the
  international site). If the data isn't provided, write around it — do not invent numbers.
- Reference FIP only. Do not mention WPT (World Padel Tour ended in 2023).
- Renders are labelled "הדמיה" / "Visualization".

## Glossary (use exactly these)
| Concept | Hebrew | English |
|---|---|---|
| a PADELTECH location | מועדון (not "מתחם", not "סניף") | club |
| the waitlist | רשימת הפתיחה | the opening list |
| sign up to waitlist (CTA) | שמרו לי מקום | Save me a spot |
| recovery/wellness zone | הרגע שאחרי | The hour after |
| corporate/group activity | קבוצות וארגונים | Teams & groups |
| property owners page | בעלי נכסים ושותפים | Sites & partners |
| the standard | תקן FIP | FIP standard |
| a match of four | רביעייה | a four |

## CTA vocabulary (only these)
- Primary: **שמרו לי מקום** / Save me a spot
- Secondary: **איך זה יעבוד** / How it will work
- Groups: **ספרו לנו על הקבוצה** / Tell us about your group
- Partners: **הציעו נכס** / Propose a site
- Interest cards: **זה אני** / That's me  (card title carries the meaning)
Retire: "יצירת קשר" as a main CTA, "הזמינו מגרש", "רשימת פתיחה" as a bare button label.

## Navigation labels
לשחק · המועדון · קבוצות וארגונים · הרגע שאחרי · הסיפור · שותפים   |   CTA: שמרו לי מקום
Play · The club · Teams & groups · The hour after · Story · Partners   |   CTA: Save me a spot
"ישראל" is NOT a nav label and should appear as a headline at most once per page.

## Message map (homepage, top to bottom)
1. **Hero** — H: "באים לשחק." · Lead: "PADELTECH היא רשת מועדוני פאדל בינלאומית שנבנית בתקן אחד. המועדון הראשון בישראל בדרך." · CTAs: שמרו לי מקום / איך זה יעבוד
2. **Experience strip** — 6 moments, word + one full short sentence each.
3. **How it will work** — 4 steps from phone to court, framed as future ("כך זה יעבוד בפתיחה").
4. **The court** — 3–4 player-felt benefits (light, bounce, space, gear on site). Full FIP spec lives on /partners.
5. **How do you want to play** — the 4 interest cards (beginner / social / training / have a four) → signup with interest preselected.
6. **The hour after** — short teaser → /wellness.
7. **Teams & groups** — one line + CTA → /groups.
8. **Where do you want to play** — region picker → signup.
9. **Signup** — name, email, region, interest, consent. Success message promises only an update.
10. **Closer** — the brand line: "זה לא המקום שבו שוכרים מגרש. זה המקום שבאים אליו לשחק."

## English rules
- Natural British-neutral English, sentence case for headings and buttons (no ALL CAPS in source strings;
  uppercase comes from CSS `type-eyebrow` only).
- It is a translation of meaning, not of words — rewrite, don't transliterate the Hebrew rhythm.

## Forms & microcopy
- Labels are nouns ("דוא״ל", "אזור מועדף"); placeholders are examples, never instructions.
- Errors say what to do: "נא להזין כתובת דוא״ל, למשל name@mail.com".
- Consent checkboxes are unchecked by default and link to /privacy.
- Success: "תודה, שמרנו לכם מקום. נעדכן לפני כולם כשיהיו פרטים על המועדון באזור שלכם."
